Did you change the appearance rate? In my experience that particular
spellbook seems to show up only rarely. Checking the spoiler seems to
indicate that in vanilla the only thing rarer is Finger of Death, and
Create Familiar shows up about as often as Polymorph. I do think it's
a really interesting spell for an early/early-mid-game character at
level 3 ... if you can find one by then. But if you haven't changed
the frequency, that may be one reason why you're not seeing people use
it. :)

Also, as the game goes on I think it becomes less interesting. The
level 6 success rate and power drain weren't the only issues with the
spell. As you get farther into the game, if all you're looking for is
to fill nearby squares with something unthreatening, there's easier
ways to do that quickly, and if you're looking for an interesting pet,
there's easier ways to do that too.

I've sometimes thought one way to make create familiar more compelling
would be to make it a bit more the player analogue of "summon nasties"
-- with something like a 1/3 chance of summoning a powerful pet from
the nasties list (or the divine minion list, or some other interesting
list), and 2/3 chance of a random. Or perhaps some other division of
probabilities based on caster and skill level. Perhaps summoning count
could be affected by caster/skill level as well. This would certainly
make it a more interesting level 6 spell.

That said, I think swapping it with charm monster was also good
decision. Charm monster is overpowered at level 3, create familiar  is
underpowered at level 6.



